      "line": 1442,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1443,
      "text": "\\section{Atlas of the \\HI\\ observations}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1444,
      "text": "\\label{thefigures}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1445,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1446,
      "text": "In the next pages overview figures are presented with the \\HI\\ data"
    },
    {
      "line": 1447,
      "text": "for all the galaxies in the sample. For each galaxy a figure is given"
    },
    {
      "line": 1448,
      "text": "with six panels. The \\HI\\ data shown are at $30''$ resolution."
    },
    {
      "line": 1449,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1450,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Top left.} A grayscale representation of the integrated"
    },
    {
      "line": 1451,
      "text": "\\HI\\ distribution.  The contour levels are $1, 2, 5, 8, 11, 15, 20,"
    },
    {
      "line": 1452,
      "text": "30, 40, 50,$ ... $10^{20}$ atoms cm$^{-2}$. The outermost contour"
    },
    {
      "line": 1453,
      "text": "always represents a column density of $1\\times 10^{20}$ atoms cm$^{-2}$."
    },
    {
      "line": 1454,
      "text": "Contours representing column densities of $5\\cdot 10^{21}$ atoms"
    },
    {
      "line": 1455,
      "text": "cm$^{-2}$ or higher are displayed in white.  The thick solid line"
    },
    {
      "line": 1456,
      "text": "gives the approximate three sigma level, determined as described in"
    },
    {
      "line": 1457,
      "text": "Sect.~\\ref{thereduction}. The plus sign indicates the position of"
    },
    {
      "line": 1458,
      "text": "the optical center.  The beam size is given in the lower left."
    },
    {
      "line": 1459,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1460,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Top right.} The velocity field. The thick line is the"
    },
    {
      "line": 1461,
      "text": "systemic velocity. The interval between the thin lines is given in the"
    },
    {
      "line": 1462,
      "text": "lower left. Light shading indicates receding velocities, dark shading"
    },
    {
      "line": 1463,
      "text": "indicates approaching velocities. The extent of the velocity field may"
    },
    {
      "line": 1464,
      "text": "be smaller than that of the integrated \\HI\\ map, because velocities"
    },
    {
      "line": 1465,
      "text": "were only determined from profiles with a signal-to-noise ratio higher"
    },
    {
      "line": 1466,
      "text": "than three."
    },
    {
      "line": 1467,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1468,
      "text": "%\\vfill"
    },
    {
      "line": 1469,
      "text": "%"
    },
    {
      "line": 1470,
      "text": "%\\hspace{-0.5cm}\\hbox to\\textwidth{"
    },
    {
      "line": 1471,
      "text": "%\\vtop{\\hbox{\\resizebox{0.5\\textwidth}{!}{\\includegraphics{h3074f13.ps}}}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1472,
      "text": "%}\\hfil"
    },
    {
      "line": 1473,
      "text": "%\\vtop{\\hbox{\\resizebox{0.5\\textwidth}{!}{\\includegraphics{h3074f14.ps}}}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1474,
      "text": "%}}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1475,
      "text": "%\\vspace{0.4cm}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1476,
      "text": "%"
    },
    {
      "line": 1477,
      "text": "%\\break"
    },
    {
      "line": 1478,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1479,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Middle left.} The integrated \\HI\\ distribution overlayed"
    },
    {
      "line": 1480,
      "text": "on the optical $R$-band image from Paper~II."
    },
    {
      "line": 1481,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1482,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Middle right.} The position-velocity diagram along the"
    },
    {
      "line": 1483,
      "text": "major axis. Contour levels are at $-4$ and $-2$ (dotted),"
    },
    {
      "line": 1484,
      "text": "and $2\\sigma$, $4\\sigma$, ... ."
    },
    {
      "line": 1485,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1486,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Bottom left.} The radial \\HI\\ density profile. The thin"
    },
    {
      "line": 1487,
      "text": "solid line gives the profile for the approaching side, the dotted line"
    },
    {
      "line": 1488,
      "text": "gives the profile for the receding side. The thick solid line is the"
    },
    {
      "line": 1489,
      "text": "average radial \\HI\\ density profile. The vertical arrow indicates a"
    },
    {
      "line": 1490,
      "text": "radius of 3.2 optical disk scale lengths."
    },
    {
      "line": 1491,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1492,
      "text": "\\noindent {\\it Bottom right.}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1493,
      "text": "The global profile. The arrow indicates the systemic velocity."
    },
    {
      "line": 1494,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "line": 1495,
      "text": "\\vspace{1cm}"
    },
    {
      "line": 1496,
      "text": ""
